WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:15.473
Hey there, my name is Ben, and I was just playing a little song I wrote for a Peanuts,

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:19.019
Earth Day special, called It’s The Small Things, Charlie Brown.

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:23.732
It’s about friendship, coming together and taking care of the place we call home.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.317
I was wondering, would you like to learn a bit of the song?

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:28.028
Yay!

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.488
Great. Okay, let’s look at the melody here.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:32.532
♪ “It’s the small things.” ♪

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:40.498
Simple, that is a G, A, B, back to G.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.792
So you can do it with these three fingers if you want.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:46.171
Or...

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.760
♪ “It’s the small things.” ♪

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.138
You know, when I was writing this song, something funny occurred to me.

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:59.434
The show is all about small things coming together to make something greater and it

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:03.521
really made me think of music and songs because that’s exactly how they work.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:08.902
Notes coming together to make chords, and melodies. Small things becoming big things.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.322
And that thought is going to take us right into the next part.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:14.407
All right, let’s see what you got.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:19.621
♪ “We come together to make big things.” ♪

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:24.209
Well that’s a few more notes. So maybe you want to lay your hands like this. See that?

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:34.511
You can start with an E. So E, D, C, B, A, C, B, A, A.

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:43.603
♪  “We come together to make big things.” ♪

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.689
If you don’t get it the first time, don’t worry about it.

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.692
Perhaps you should try a different approach.

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:53.238
You can go back and try again as much as you want to that’s what we call practice.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:57.742
Now if you don’t have a piano that’s no problem, you can be the percussionist,

00:01:57.742 --> 00:02:00.161
which is what I was when I was when I was growing up.

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:03.373
And a percussionist is the person who pounds on 

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:06.459
things to keep the beat or the rhythm of the song.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:08.837
Now, there are all kinds of percussion instruments.

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:13.383
I used to use basketballs and coffee cans ‘cause I didn’t have a drum set.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:17.011
But you can snap, clap, whatever you want to do.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:19.889
And when the music starts, just tap along with the beat.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.642
I’m going to use this tambourine right here.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:23.977
Hit it!

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:48.585
That’s great, you’re doing great. We really found our groove.

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:54.424
Charlie Brown, Charlie Brown, Charlie Brown!

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.302
Now I don’t know about you but I can’t wait to watch

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:58.887
It’s a Small Things, Charlie Brown.

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:00.180
I think you are going to love it.

